There's no item, other than the Amulet, that restricts your teleport
ability in any way.  My first guess is that you've discovered the
castle level, as that is a well-known feature of the castle level.

>I cannot seem to find the stairway leading downward. I though the Hell
>levels did not have down stairs. I have read an uncursed map of magic
>mapping and it did not point the way to the down stairway.

If you are on the castle level, you've probably discovered a large
water-filled moat surrounding the castle itself.  There are no down
staircases on or below the castle level.  There are ways to get down,
though...

Spoilers follow

Exploring the castle will reveal a series of trap doors in the back,
leading down to the first level of Hell.  If you want to go deeper
(and you will), you will have to try another way.

If you have teleport control and you either step on a level teleport
trap or read a cursed scroll of level teleport, you will be queried
for the level to be teleported to.  The deepest you could possibly go
this way is level 50, which is almost certainly deeper than the
Wizard.

There are ways to get an idea of what level the Wizard is on, but
they're beyond the scope of this article.


